        <TR>
          <TD class=3D"labelCell">Jurisdiction:</TD>
          <TD>Victoria</TD></TR>
        <TR>
          <TD class=3D"labelCell">Abstract:</TD>
          <TD>Victorian Land Cover provides a consistent through time,=20
            whole-of-state, spatial land cover data set for 7 epochs =
(1987-1990,=20
            1990-1995, 1995-2000, 2000-2005, 2005-2010, 2010-2015 and =
2015-19).=20
            The dataset uses Landsat satellite imagery and local =
calibration (or=20
            training) data. The most likely layers (one for each epoch) =
classify=20
            each pixel in to one of 19 land cover classes. The dataset =
provides=20
            additional evidence for use alongside other South Australian =
mapping=20
            products to measure and map native and non-native land cover =
types=20
            (although land cover types delineated are different between=20
          States).</TD></TR>
        <TR>
          <TD class=3D"labelCell">Search Words:</TD>
          <TD>LAND Cover, VEGETATION</TD></TR>
        <TR>
          <TD class=3D"labelCell">Purpose:</TD>
          <TD>This dataset can be used to inform spatial and temporal=20
            (5-yearly) summaries of the described land cover types for =
Victoria.=20
            The capture method and general nature of the classes are =
most useful=20
            for landscape and regional scale assessment (1:50,000 scale =
or=20
            smaller). Localised or paddock scale applications may =
encounter=20
            classification errors as a result of the modelling method =
that=20
            characterises spectral similarity. Note: it should not be =
assumed=20
            that this dataset represents a definitive land cover class =
at any=20
            given pixel, rather it aims to provide a consistent spectral =

            description of land covers through time / between epochs. =
Associated=20
            datasets can be obtained by contacting the Data Authority =
where the=20
            class definitions, spatial resolution and five year time =
intervals=20
            are appropriate for a particular type of analysis or =
application.=20
        </TD></TR>
